            <ArticleTitle>Absence of Dermatitis Among Rubber Plantation Workers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>292</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>None of the 40 rubber plantation workers exposed to latex for many years examined by us, had developed any significant dermatitis apart from thickening and lichenification of the dorsal aspect of right index finger and medial aspect of right thumb.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
